<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.170 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.170 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE AUG 31, 1998</p>
<p>			     $18.752 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.170    Awarded At	99.917	6.125</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.150    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.119    21 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.23 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Aug.98</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 03.Sep.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 27.Aug.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  18.752 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912827Z21</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   41.737			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.517				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.125</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   2.350			   PRICE	 99.917</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.119-6.170 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.170</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.288 PCT AT AUCTION ON 23.JUL.96</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.053 PCT AT AUCTION 29.MAY.96</p>
</text>
